	(text "Charlieplexed button reading procedure:\n1. Set all pin to ANALOG in,\n    except for one row to output HIGH\n2. Wait until the pin state settles\n3. Read all ANALOG pin for button detection\n4. Repeat for all rows\n\nReason to use red LED:\nAnti-ghosting measurement.\nThe point is not the light itself.\nIt has optimal voltage drop of ~1.7V,\neasy to tell 1 vs 2 red LED being passed thru."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 232.918 96.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "15f6329e-7f2d-4fcb-9723-1c6818fef46c")
	)
